invariant: INV-22
file: handshake_record.c
catches: unit
reason: hsr_refuse_alert no longer records the peer's fatal alert, so
  ch_alert_received reads 0 and the failure funnel, which sends nothing only
  once that field is set, answers the peer's alert with one of its own.
  bin/unit requires the description and no send call.

--- old
        t->alert_received = pt[1];
--- new
        (void)t;
